│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current highly-symmetric “collective RX/RY output mixer” with a slightly more │
│                          │ expressive, still parameter-efficient structure:                                          │
│                          │ - Keep the input collective RY and collective RZ.                                         │
│                          │ - Keep the cube entangling CZ network (12 CZs).                                           │
│                          │ - Add one additional parameterized controlled-phase layer (CRZ) on a disjoint matching of │
│                          │ 4 pairs (reuses a single shared parameter for all four CRZ gates).                        │
│                          │ - Use a single collective Y-basis mixer for all qubits (to rotate into the measured Z     │
│                          │ basis) plus one collective final Z rotation, instead of both collective RY and collective │
│                          │ RX.                                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This increases ansatz expressivity (non-diagonal + additional entangling                  │
│                          │ non-commutativity via CRZ) while increasing parameter count only from 4→5 per block,      │
│                          │ which should improve validation/test accuracy and reduce the train-test gap without       │
│                          │ overfitting.                                                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
