│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shinkaevolve8_hypercube_cr_shared                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replaces the previous highly-shared ansatz with a more                                    │
│                          │ expressive-but-still-parameter-efficient block.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes inside <EVOLVE-BLOCK>:                                                        │
│                          │ - Uses two shared “input” rotation parameters for the lower half qubits (0–3) and upper   │
│                          │ half (4–7), instead of one fully collective parameter. This increases representational    │
│                          │ capacity while keeping parameter count low.                                               │
│                          │ - Adds one shared parametrized controlled layer (CRZ + CRX) on a structured matching      │
│                          │ between lower/upper halves to better exploit noncommuting interactions without exploding  │
│                          │ the parameter count.                                                                      │
│                          │ - Keeps the fixed CZ entangling structure (cube-like) to maintain strong inductive bias   │
│                          │ for binary-feature parity correlations.                                                   │
│                          │ - Uses two shared “output” mixers (RY and RX) split across halves to improve the mapping  │
│                          │ from learned phases to the fixed Z readout.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ No changes are made outside the EVOLVE-BLOCK: training loop, feature map, re-uploading,   │
│                          │ parameter handling, and measurements remain identical.                                    │
